{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2007-12-13","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2017-02-22","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Sparacino, Cristiana Ms","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"\"The project's development objective is to contribute to rural poverty reduction and food security through improved access to, and management of, water resources for agricultural and pastoral use. Specific objectives are to: (i) strengthen target group capacities and facilitate their participation in project activities, including through access to irrigated land; (ii) assist target groups with investments to increase their access to irrigation water using technologies adapted to their technical skills and resource levels; (iii) intensify and diversify sustainable agricultural production under irrigation and in inland valley bottoms; and (iv) support marketing activities and enhance incomes, particularly of the most asset-poor households.\nPolicy objectives include contributing to the body of best practices for sustainable, pro-poor interventions in irrigated smallholder agriculture in the framework of the recently approved national policy for the sustainable development of irrigated agriculture. Institutional objectives include strengthening technical capacity in the small-scale irrigation subsector at the grass-roots level and in central and deconcentrated line agencies. The former includes irrigator committees, water user associations, and similar grass-roots and farmer organizations; the latter, the Directorate for Irrigation Development (DDI) and the recently established Directorate for Rural Land Tenure Security and Farmer Organizations (DGFROP).\"The project''s development objective is to contribute to rural poverty reduction and food security through improved access to, and management of, water resources for agricultural and pastoral use. Specific objectives are to: (i) strengthen target group capacities and facilitate their participation in project activities, including through access to irrigated land; (ii) assist target groups with investments to increase their access to irrigation water using technologies adapted to their technical skills and resource levels; (iii) intensify and diversify sustainable agricultural production under irrigation and in inland valley bottoms; and (iv) support marketing activities and enhance incomes, particularly of the most asset-poor households.Policy objectives include contributing to the body of best practices for sustainable, pro-poor interventions in irrigated smallholder agriculture in the framework of the recently approved national policy for the sustainable development of irrigated agriculture. Institutional objectives include strengthening technical capacity in the small-scale irrigation subsector at the grass-roots level and in central and deconcentrated line agencies. The former includes irrigator committees, water user associations, and similar grass-roots and farmer organizations; the latter, the Directorate for Irrigation Development (DDI) and the recently established Directorate for Rural Land Tenure Security and Farmer Organizations (DGFROP).","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of development.","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"IATI documentation on IFAD corporate website","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"TEXT/HTML","@url":"/en/iati"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"